      "content": "thanks. looking at what you wrote, the scientific side feels really solid and based on these heavy ethical and community-focused concepts. but with the civil liberties part, it feels a bit more like they're just worried about the principle of it? like, does the scientific community have a way to directly address the actual health claims or the validity of the liberty concerns, or is it mostly just a clash of \"science vs freedom\"?",
